.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt SLEEP 1
.Os NovaOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm sleep
.Nd wait for the sum of the durations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl
.Ar duration ...
.Nm
.Fl Fl help | Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A duration is a nonnegative decimal or hexadecimal number, optionally followed by
s, m, h or d for seconds, minutes, hours or days. The default unit is seconds.
Use inf to wait indefinitely. The first recognized option takes effect immediately.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl sleep .025 1e-3s
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, one for invalid input or an error during the wait.
.Sh RIGHTS
Documentation needs only output. A positive wait in NovaOS uses a private IPC
endpoint. The command does not read stdin or access files.
